From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:41:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] msdaps: the OLE DB proxies and stubs that were stubs (3190)

IRowPosition and IRowPositionChange, IChapteredRowset, IGetDataSource, IColumnsInfo, IColumnsRowset,
IConvertType, ICommandPrepare, ICommandWithParameters, ICommandProperties, ITransactionJoin/Local/
Object, IRowsetIdentity, IMultipleResults, IOpenRowset, IAccessor::GetBindings and
IDBProperties::GetPropertyInfo / IDBDataSourceAdmin::GetCreationProperties now marshal like the
other OLE DB interfaces: the proxy calls the Remote method and hands the error info to the caller,
the stub calls the real method and passes a failure's error info back, property statuses are copied
both ways, and rowsets returned by OpenRowset, GetColumnsRowset and GetResult go through the rowset
server as Execute's do (the provider's success code is kept).

Column names, parameter names and property descriptions that point into one string buffer travel as
the buffer and an offset for each pointer. The wire length of that buffer is a ULONG: widl shares
one size callback between the arrays of a function, so GetColumnInfo / GetParameterInfo sent the
string buffer with the length of the column array; colinf.idl and cmdwpr.idl now give the length a
type that needs no callback. GetCreationProperties' stub now fills the offsets its proxy needs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
